/** \page jam-prebuilt-page Prebuilt Dependencies

A Jam project can take third-party libraries from a prebuilt dependency bundle
instead of from the system or from sources in the tree. A bundle is a directory
of already compiled headers and libraries for one platform. The published
bundles might include zlib, libpng, libjpeg, FreeType or OpenSSL.

The bundle is placed under the @c prebuilt directory in the project root. Each
platform has its own subdirectory, for example @c prebuilt/windows-x64-msvc-md.
Those files contain no absolute paths, so the directory can be moved or unpacked
as a whole.

Prebuilt libraries are used only when passing @c --with-prebuilt or
@c --fetch-prebuilt. They do not replace the compiler, and they do not change
the global compiler or linker flags. See @ref jam-usage for the rest of the
configure and build process.

@section jam-prebuilt-page-Using Using Prebuilt Dependencies

The usual first-time command downloads the matching bundle if needed, then
configures the build:

@code
jam.bat configure --fetch-prebuilt
./jam.sh configure --fetch-prebuilt
@endcode

If the bundle is already on disk, pass @c --with-prebuilt instead. Jam picks
the platform folder from the current OS, CPU and toolset. The command fails if
that folder is missing. No network access is performed.

@code
./jam.sh configure --with-prebuilt
@endcode

Either flag may take an explicit platform name. That pins the folder under
@c prebuilt, still without downloading with @c --with-prebuilt:

@code
./jam.sh configure --with-prebuilt=windows-x64-msvc-md
./jam.sh configure --with-prebuilt=macos-arm64-clang
./jam.sh configure --fetch-prebuilt=windows-x64-msvc-md
@endcode

@c --fetch-prebuilt already selects prebuilt libraries; @c --with-prebuilt is
not required next to it. Do not combine @c --fetch-prebuilt with
@c --with-prebuilt=name. Fetch always writes into the platform folder under
@c prebuilt. A stale folder is refreshed only by @c --fetch-prebuilt;
@c --with-prebuilt will not contact the network.

The platform folder name is @c os-arch-toolset, with an extra suffix on
Windows. Jam builds it from @c TARGET_OS, @c TARGET_OSPLAT and @c TOOLSET:

- @c nt / @c win32 become @c windows; @c macosx becomes @c macos
- @c x86_64 / @c amd64 become @c x64; @c aarch64 becomes @c arm64
- Visual Studio toolsets @c vc* become @c msvc

Examples:

- @c windows-x64-msvc-md
- @c windows-x64-msvc-mdd
- @c macos-arm64-clang
- @c linux-x64-clang

Windows always has a suffix for the C runtime. A debug build without
optimization maps to @c mdd, otherwise @c md. Other operating systems omit the
suffix until a second runtime variant exists. The project's debug/release
setting and that Windows suffix are separate: on Linux and macOS the same
folder is used for both debug and release builds.

The default location is @c prebuilt/<name> in the project root. The download
uses the release tag @c PREBUILT_RELEASE (default @c prebuilt-1). The zip URL
is:

@verbatim
https://github.com/Pt-Framework/Pt/releases/download/<PREBUILT_RELEASE>/<name>.zip
@endverbatim

Settings made explicitly always win. If any of the five package variables
are set on the command line or in the environment, or if a flag is passed
that builds that package from sources in the tree, prebuilt paths are not
applied to that package. The following commands keep a hand-chosen zlib or
build zlib from sources, while still using the bundle for the other libraries:

@code
./jam.sh configure --with-prebuilt -sZLIB_INCLUDES=/opt/zlib/include
./jam.sh configure --fetch-prebuilt --with-inline-zlib
@endcode

Flags such as @c --with-inline-zlib, @c --with-inline-libpng,
@c --with-inline-libjpeg and @c --with-inline-freetype skip the corresponding
Configure probe and build that package from sources in the tree.

Configure looks for each library in this order:

@verbatim
User settings / --with-inline-xxx
        |
        |  else, if a prebuilt folder was selected
        v
Prebuilt paths  ->  one package Configure probe
        |
        |  else (prebuilt not selected), or probe failed
        v
System / compiler paths / pkg-config
        |
        |  else
        v
Sources in the tree
@endverbatim

When prebuilt libraries are selected, the system is not consulted for packages
listed in the bundle. When they are not selected, @c prebuilt is not consulted
at all. There is no fallback from one platform folder to another. If the chosen
folder is missing, configure reports an error. If a package probe against the
bundle fails, that package falls back to sources in the tree.

@section jam-prebuilt-page-Layout Layout

One platform is one directory and one zip. Each library lives in its own
subdirectory, named after @c PREBUILT_PACKAGES (@c zlib, @c png, @c jpeg,
@c freetype, @c openssl).

@verbatim
prebuilt/<name>/
  jam/
    packages.jam
  zlib/
    include/zlib.h
    lib/zlib.lib          (or libz.a / libz.dylib)
    bin/zlib.dll          (omitted for static)
  png/
    include/png.h
    lib/png16.lib
    bin/libpng16.dll
  jpeg/
    include/...
    lib/...
    bin/...
  freetype/
    include/ft2build.h
    include/freetype2/...
    lib/freetype.lib
    bin/freetype.dll
  openssl/
    include/openssl/...
    lib/libssl.lib libcrypto.lib
    bin/...
@endverbatim

Default locations, relative to @c PREBUILT_ROOT:

- Headers: @c $(pkg)/include
- Libraries: @c $(pkg)/lib
- Binaries: @c $(pkg)/bin

@c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_INCLUDES.$(pkg) is set only when that layout is not enough
(FreeType's @c include/freetype2). The native @c lib/ and @c bin/ directories
are kept complete. There are no version directories and no @c debug/ folder
inside an @c md tree. Library names stay the same for a given platform folder
(@c zlib.lib in both @c md and @c mdd).

The directory can be moved as a whole because it contains no absolute paths.
The project sets @c PREBUILT_ROOT before including @c jam/packages.jam.

@section jam-prebuilt-page-Manifest packages.jam

Each bundle contains one Jam data file at @c jam/packages.jam. It assigns
variables only: no rules and no toolset flags. The rules that use those
variables live in @c jam/prebuilt.jam.

Names that describe the whole bundle use the prefix @c PREBUILT_. Names that
vary by package use @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_ plus a dotted package name, for
example @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_LIBS.zlib, which is read as
@c $(PREBUILT_PACKAGE_LIBS.$(pkg)).

Bundle-wide variables:

- @c PREBUILT_SCHEMA is the file format version. The project requires @c 1.
- @c PREBUILT_ID is the same string as the directory and zip name.
- @c PREBUILT_LINKAGE is @c shared or @c static. @c Prebuilt-LinkLibs uses
  this when deciding whether to also link packages that this one depends on.
- @c PREBUILT_PACKAGES lists the package names that have dotted keys.

Per-package variables. Omit empty lists. Values are names, tokens, or paths
relative to @c PREBUILT_ROOT, never raw flags (@c -l, @c -I, @c -D,
@c -framework, @c /LIBPATH):

- @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_LIBS.$(pkg): library names inside the bundle
  (@c zlib, @c png16, @c ssl @c crypto). Not @c -lssl or @c zlib.lib.
- @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_DEPENDS.$(pkg): other packages in this bundle that
  this one needs.
- @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_SYSLIBS.$(pkg): OS linker names that are not in the zip
  (@c crypt32, @c ws2_32). Jam applies @c FLinkLibs.
- @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_FRAMEWORKS.$(pkg): macOS framework names.
- @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_DEFINES.$(pkg): preprocessor tokens, not @c -D.
- @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_INCLUDES.$(pkg): include paths relative to
  @c PREBUILT_ROOT, only if not @c $(pkg)/include.
- @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_LIBPATH.$(pkg): library paths relative to
  @c PREBUILT_ROOT, only if not @c $(pkg)/lib.
- @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_LINKFLAGS.$(pkg): extra linker flags.
- @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_VERSION.$(pkg): version string for documentation.

@c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_DEPENDS lists every needed package in the same bundle. If
png is in the bundle, zlib is in the bundle too. The project walks that list
for include paths (always), for files to copy (when asked), and for extra
link libraries (static linking only). There are no version ranges, no optional
dependencies, and no search for a package outside the bundle.

The file does not set @c ZLIB_LINKLIBS or @c SSL_LINKLIBS. Mapping package
names to those project variables is done in @c jam/prebuilt.jam.

Example:

@code
# prebuilt/<name>/jam/packages.jam
if ! $(PREBUILT_PACKAGES_JAM_INCLUDED) {
PREBUILT_PACKAGES_JAM_INCLUDED = true ;

PREBUILT_SCHEMA  = 1 ;
PREBUILT_ID      = windows-x64-msvc-md ;
PREBUILT_LINKAGE = shared ;

PREBUILT_PACKAGES = zlib png jpeg freetype openssl ;

PREBUILT_PACKAGE_LIBS.zlib        = zlib ;
PREBUILT_PACKAGE_VERSION.zlib     = 1.3.1 ;

PREBUILT_PACKAGE_LIBS.png         = png16 ;
PREBUILT_PACKAGE_DEPENDS.png      = zlib ;
PREBUILT_PACKAGE_VERSION.png      = 1.6.43 ;

PREBUILT_PACKAGE_LIBS.jpeg        = jpeg ;
PREBUILT_PACKAGE_VERSION.jpeg     = 3.0.3 ;

PREBUILT_PACKAGE_LIBS.freetype    = freetype ;
PREBUILT_PACKAGE_DEPENDS.freetype = png zlib ;
PREBUILT_PACKAGE_VERSION.freetype = 2.13.2 ;

PREBUILT_PACKAGE_LIBS.openssl     = ssl crypto ;
PREBUILT_PACKAGE_SYSLIBS.openssl  = crypt32 ws2_32 advapi32 user32 ;
PREBUILT_PACKAGE_VERSION.openssl  = 3.3.1 ;

}
@endcode

A macOS bundle uses a three-part @c PREBUILT_ID such as @c macos-arm64-clang.
The Windows @c mdd folder uses @c PREBUILT_ID = windows-x64-msvc-mdd, the same
linkage, and different files on disk.

@section jam-prebuilt-page-Configure Configure Integration

Every package Configure rule has the same arguments:

@verbatim
*-Configure INCLUDES : C++FLAGS : LINKLIBS : LIBDIR : LINKFLAGS
@endverbatim

If any of those is set, pkg-config is skipped and the first link attempt uses
the passed libraries. If all five are empty, pkg-config and name
guessing run. On success the five @c *_ variables are set.

@c Prebuilt-Import sets @c PREBUILT_ROOT and includes @c jam/packages.jam. It
does not touch @c C++FLAGS, @c LINKFLAGS, or @c ZLIB_*.

For each package, if the bundle is loaded and sources in the tree were not
requested, empty variables are filled from the bundle, then Configure is
called once:

@code
Load zlib.jam ;

if --with-inline-zlib in $(ARGV)
{
    WITH_BUILTIN_ZLIB = yes ;
}

if ! $(WITH_BUILTIN_ZLIB)
{
    if $(PREBUILT_ROOT)
    {
        ZLIB_INCLUDES  ?= [ Prebuilt-Includes zlib ] ;
        ZLIB_C++FLAGS  ?= [ Prebuilt-CxxFlags zlib ] ;
        ZLIB_LINKLIBS  ?= [ Prebuilt-LinkLibs zlib ] ;
        ZLIB_LIBDIR    ?= [ Prebuilt-LibPath zlib ] ;
        ZLIB_LINKFLAGS ?= [ Prebuilt-LinkFlags zlib ] ;
    }

    WITH_ZLIB = [ ZLib-Configure $(ZLIB_INCLUDES) : $(ZLIB_C++FLAGS) :
                                 $(ZLIB_LINKLIBS) : $(ZLIB_LIBDIR) : $(ZLIB_LINKFLAGS) ] ;
}

if ! $(WITH_ZLIB)
{
    WITH_BUILTIN_ZLIB = yes ;
}
@endcode

The same pattern is used for png (@c PNG_*), jpeg (@c JPEG_*), FreeType
(@c FREETYPE_*), and OpenSSL. The zip package name is @c openssl; the Jam
variables stay @c SSL_*, as @c OpenSsl-Configure already uses. Flags that
select sources in the tree are handled before the prebuilt or system probe.

Package name to variable mapping:

- @c zlib -> @c ZLIB_*
- @c png -> @c PNG_*
- @c jpeg -> @c JPEG_*
- @c freetype -> @c FREETYPE_*
- @c openssl -> @c SSL_*

@c *_LIBDIR is required. Setting only @c *_LINKLIBS leaves the linker without
@c FLibPath of the package's @c lib/ directory. @c CheckDependencyLinkC++
turns @c LIBDIR into @c *_LINKFLAGS.

Jamfiles do not mention @c PREBUILT_ROOT. They keep using the five package
variables:

@code
SubDirHdrs $(PNG_INCLUDES) ;
LinkFlags mylib : $(PNG_LINKFLAGS) ;
LinkLibs  mylib : $(PNG_LINKLIBS) ;
ObjectC++Flags PngReader.cpp PngWriter.cpp : $(PNG_C++FLAGS) ;
@endcode

Whether a package was found or built from sources is still the usual
@c WITH_* / @c WITH_BUILTIN_* variables, as without prebuilt libraries.

Include directories always cover dependent packages as well. @c png.h includes
@c zlib.h, and a Jamfile can call @c SubDirHdrs $(PNG_INCLUDES) without adding
@c ZLIB_INCLUDES. Therefore @c Prebuilt-Includes png returns @c png/include
and @c zlib/include. That walk follows @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_DEPENDS for both
shared and static bundles. @c Prebuilt-Includes freetype returns FreeType's
include dirs plus png and zlib.

Link lines do not always add dependent packages:

- Shared: @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_LIBS and @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_SYSLIBS of the
  named packages only, plus @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_FRAMEWORKS as
  @c -framework name
- Static: the same, after also collecting the packages listed in
  @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_DEPENDS
- MSVC shared OpenSSL still needs @c crypt32 @c ws2_32 @c advapi32 @c user32
  on the line (@c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_SYSLIBS)

@section jam-prebuilt-page-API Jam Rules

The rules live in @c jam/prebuilt.jam, loaded once per project. The bundle
file is @c jam/packages.jam. Toolset helpers stay in the project:
@c FLinkLibs, @c FIncludes, @c FDefines, @c FLibPath.

- @c Prebuilt-Tuple ( abi ? ) \n
  Builds the platform folder name from @c TARGET_OS, @c TARGET_OSPLAT and
  @c TOOLSET, with an optional extra suffix such as @c md.

- @c Prebuilt-Fetch ( url : dest ) \n
  Downloads @c url when the remote @c url.manifest differs from
  @c dest/manifest. Replaces @c dest with the unzipped archive. The caller
  must run @c Fetch-Configure first.

- @c Prebuilt-Import ( root ) \n
  Sets @c PREBUILT_ROOT, includes @c jam/packages.jam, and exits if
  @c PREBUILT_SCHEMA is not @c 1.

- @c Prebuilt-Depends ( packages + ) \n
  Walks @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_DEPENDS without duplicates. Named packages first,
  dependencies last.

- @c Prebuilt-Includes ( packages + ) \n
  Include directories of those packages and the packages they depend on. Uses
  @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_INCLUDES.$(pkg) when set, otherwise
  @c $(PREBUILT_ROOT)/$(pkg)/include.

- @c Prebuilt-CxxFlags ( packages + ) \n
  @c [ FDefines $(PREBUILT_PACKAGE_DEFINES.$(pkg)) ] for the named packages
  only.

- @c Prebuilt-LinkLibs ( packages + ) \n
  Shared: @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_LIBS, @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_SYSLIBS and
  @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_FRAMEWORKS of the named packages. Static: the same
  over the packages returned by @c Prebuilt-Depends. Always passed through
  @c FLinkLibs. Frameworks are appended as @c -framework name.

- @c Prebuilt-LibPath ( packages + ) \n
  @c $(PREBUILT_ROOT)/$(pkg)/lib, or @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_LIBPATH.$(pkg).
  Shared: named packages. Static: those packages and the ones they depend on.

- @c Prebuilt-LinkFlags ( packages + ) \n
  Extra flags from @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_LINKFLAGS.$(pkg) only. Does not
  duplicate @c FLibPath; @c CheckDependencyLinkC++ adds that from @c LIBDIR.

- @c Prebuilt-Packages \n
  All package names exported by the bundle (@c PREBUILT_PACKAGES).

- @c Prebuilt-Bin ( packages + ) / @c Prebuilt-Lib ( packages + ) \n
  All files below the native @c bin/ or @c lib/ directory of each named
  package. These rules do not walk dependencies.

@section jam-prebuilt-page-Deploy Deployment

Prebuilt bundles keep complete native @c bin/ and @c lib/ directories. They do
not say which files to install. A package @c bin/ can contain programs as well
as runtime libraries; Linux and macOS shared libraries commonly remain in
@c lib/.

The project chooses which packages to copy and whether to take @c bin/ or
@c lib/, then stages or installs with its own rules. For every package:

@code
local packages = [ Prebuilt-Packages ] ;
local sources = [ Prebuilt-Bin $(packages) ] ;
sources += [ Prebuilt-Lib $(packages) ] ;

for local src in $(sources)
{
    local dest = $(src:BS) ;
    File $(dest) : $(src) ;
    MakeLocate $(dest) : $(LOCATE_TARGET) ;
    Clean clean : $(dest) ;
    InstallFile $(BINDIR) : $(src) ;
}
@endcode

For a smaller set, pass package names to @c Prebuilt-Bin or @c Prebuilt-Lib.
To include files from packages that one of them depends on, first use
@c local packages = [ Prebuilt-Depends openssl ] ;.

@note Windows @c mdd is not redistributable. The debug CRT
(@c MSVCP*D.dll, @c VCRUNTIME*D.dll) is not in the Visual C++
redistributable. Release products use @c md. Local debug builds may place
@c mdd DLLs next to the executable.

@section jam-prebuilt-page-Produce Creating Prebuilt Dependencies

A bundle can be written by hand: fill the per-package directories, write
@c jam/packages.jam, and point @c --with-prebuilt at the platform folder
under @c prebuilt. Conan is not required. @c packages.jam is @c KEY = value
assignments and is readable without running Jam.

A generator, including one driven by Conan in CI, writes the same layout:

- One directory per package: @c $(pkg)/include, @c $(pkg)/lib, @c $(pkg)/bin
- @c jam/packages.jam: library names to @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_LIBS, other
  packages in this bundle to @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_DEPENDS, OS linker names to
  @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_SYSLIBS, macOS frameworks to
  @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_FRAMEWORKS, extra include dirs to
  @c PREBUILT_PACKAGE_INCLUDES
- Complete @c lib/ and @c bin/ directories, without sorting or moving files
- Do not emit @c ZLIB_INCLUDES / @c PNG_LINKLIBS from the generator; that
  mapping is @c jam/prebuilt.jam
- Windows: two zips, @c windows-x64-msvc-md and @c windows-x64-msvc-mdd
- macOS / Linux: one folder name without a runtime suffix until a second
  variant exists
- Check: @c zlib/include/zlib.h, @c zlib/lib/zlib.lib or @c libz.a, @c bin/
  when shared, @c jam/packages.jam, no version directories, no absolute
  machine paths

*/
